title: "Loom: a measurement-based production system for Ableton Live"
type: software
version: "2.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-12"
authors:
  - family-names: "Şahan"
    given-names: "Şenol"
    affiliation: "SubverseLab"
url: "https://subverselab.com/loom"
repository-code: "https://github.com/senolsahan037-oss/loom"
license: "LicenseRef-AllRightsReserved"
keywords:
  - "Ableton Live"
  - "Model Context Protocol"
  - "MCP server"
  - "music production"
  - "MIDI"
abstract: >-
  Loom is a local MCP server that connects Claude to a running Ableton Live
  session through an Ableton Extension. It reads the producer's own .als
  projects and library, answers with counts measured from that work rather
  than with guesses, and writes MIDI, device chains, automation and
  arrangement markers into Live, verifying every write by reading it back.
